A||||11||SLYGUY||Found my 88 GT||||12||
Z||000000||SLYGUY||09-07-2001||04:28 AM||||I found a 88GT here locally. $5100 out the door. Gonna post some pics as soon as possible. <P>I need a little help on some parts however. The left headlight is a little sick. Motor runs but I think the worm gear is stripped because it dances around and rarely makes it too fully deployed position. Also, left quarter window, the one with GT inscribed on it has a crack. I'll need to replace that too. Any help would be appreciated.<P>Thanks<BR>Sly||||reg||12
Z||000001||Raydar||09-07-2001||07:10 AM||||Check Rodney Dickman for the headlight bushings. Easy fix. Costs around $5. <BR>Takes about a half hour. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/index.html</A> <P>Doug McKinney sells reproduction 1/4 windows.<BR>As nice as GMs but at half the price.  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/</A> <P>Congrats on your find, and welcome to the Forum!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||09-07-2001||07:15 AM||||Welcome to the forum! You don't know it yet but you found a new home.  You can get a headlight motor rebuilding kit from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com.</A>   I got a factory original replacement quarter window <A HREF="http://www.gmpartdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartdirect.com</A>  for around $150.  There are cheaper copies available and I am sure other will tell you the web site I just don't have it right now.  Good luck and enjoy your car. <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||09-07-2001||09:18 AM||||Cool, Welcome to the forum!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif"> <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Fiero5||09-07-2001||09:42 AM||||Welcome fellow Fiero-ite<BR>Look forward to seeing the pics<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pegasuswarriersSig.jpg">                            <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000005||SLYGUY||09-07-2001||10:45 AM||||Thank you so much. Your help is greatly appreciated. Glad that those will be easy fixes.<BR>This forum is great for this car. I had an '86 SE V6. Red/Slvr and loved it. Traded it in on something I think. Oh well, this 88 is better looking!<BR>Wish it would of come with the radio/subwoofer that was in the 86!<BR>Hey, that's another question. I can see the speakers behind the occupants heads but they don't work and won't respond when you slid the fader to the rear. Any clues?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||09-07-2001||11:36 AM||||Not sure why the rear speakers don't work. I'm guessing the seller had an aftermarket radio, and reinstalled the stock one. And didn't plug in the back speakers. Never heard of a back speaker dying completely.<BR>The sun cooks the front ones, though.<P>If you want a subwoofer system, I know a friend who has one. The speaker needs to be reconed or replaced (Rodney Dickman sells those, too. Like $40.), but otherwise it's complete.<BR>Wants $100. Let me know if you're interested. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||09-07-2001||11:51 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>I can see the speakers behind the occupants heads</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you saying the speakers are in the headrests?  If that's the case, 84-85's had those and someone must have tried to add them to your '88 at one time.  The 88's never had headrest speakers so they may not work maybe because they are just not wired up.  They could be if you wanted to.<P>If it's the speakers in the interior sail piece, then you'd have to remove that whole trim piece to get to the speakers and you'll need to remove the seat belt anchor bolts.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||09-07-2001||12:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Welcome to the forum! You don't know it yet but you found a new home.  You can get a headlight motor rebuilding kit from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com.</A>   I got a factory original replacement quarter window <A HREF="http://www.gmpartdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartdirect.com</A>  for around $150.  There are cheaper copies available and I am sure other will tell you the web site I just don't have it right now.  Good luck and enjoy your car. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have you got a part number for those quarter windows?  I know a bunch of people are looking for them, but don't like the repros since they aren't curved like the factory ones.  They're very close, but for a show car you can tell the difference.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000009||SLYGUY||09-07-2001||01:44 PM||||Thanks Tigger. That was what I figured the problem was. I need to get them going and replace a blow one in the dash because I am resisting my urges to remove the stock stereo and go all out with a great system. This, of course, would ruin it's originality. I'm pretty sure that once all the speakers are working like they are supposed to that it will quench my thirst for a hi-fi setup at least temporarily!<P>Take care and thank you again for all of the help everyone.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000010||SLYGUY||09-07-2001||01:47 PM||||Raydar:<P>I ordered a pair of those rebuild kits with the bushings. I'm gonna have to wait for the quarter window. I think it would be wise to replace both at the same time so they will match in all their NON-OEM splendor. <P>I'm off to replace all four of those little light bulbs that light up the "PONTIAC" between the tailights.<P>Thanks again.<BR>Sly||||reg||14
Z||000011||skitime||09-07-2001||01:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Have you got a part number for those quarter windows?  I know a bunch of people are looking for them, but don't like the repros since they aren't curved like the factory ones.  They're very close, but for a show car you can tell the difference.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Gmpartsdirect list them for 149.08 for the left one and 141.29 for the right one. These prices are with shipping. Some reproductions are tinted but they also tint the GT emblem which I don't like. Other reproductions are clear which is not orginal either. The GM part numbers are 20701106 for the right one and 20701107 for the left. I agree that the repros are good but the original are the best especially if you show your car.<P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
